cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its experiment records, please cite it as below."
title: "Count, Don't Retrain: Keeping a Frozen Learned String Index Certified Under Inserts and Deletes"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nelapati
    given-names: Kshiraja
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-1539-9717"
  - family-names: Sayal
    given-names: Prathmesh
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-0108-1789"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pratz1337/RankTransport-Index"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - learned index
  - string index
  - rank queries
  - dynamic updates
  - certified error bound
abstract: >-
  HRT-LI freezes a piecewise-linear learned index certified on a base snapshot of byte-string
  keys and records the live set's signed difference from that snapshot in a byte-radix ledger.
  Adding the ledger's mass below a query to the model's prediction keeps the certified error of
  every surviving base key unchanged after any sequence of inserts and deletes; new keys and
  absent boundaries are answered by exact counting.
